From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 04:37:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11006/11362] The induce measurement lands: truncation fixed,
 levels did not follow

The 7-hour r11l run completed and is the first eval artifact to carry
generator_channels. Pre-fix the induce channel showed 24 of 24 completions
reasoning-only with chars_final 0; this run shows 3 of 13 reasoning-only with
chars_final 37,872 and two engines emitted. The server answered in both regimes,
so this is the model finishing rather than a connectivity difference. The
truncation fix is real and now measured rather than argued.

98.5% of generated characters are still reasoning -- 2,467,130 against 37,872 of
final output -- so an induce is dominated by thinking that is discarded.

The uncomfortable half: this morning's arm-OFF run banked 2 levels in 2121
actions, and this post-fix run banked 1 in 2077. Recorded with its caveats
rather than as a regression, since the budgets differ by 8x, both are single
samples of a stochastic search, and efficiency is not comparable across
different level counts. What it does rule out is the hopeful reading that
removing the context wall converts into levels.

Also records a side effect anyone running more evals needs: the dashboard's
generalization line dropped 5 to 4 because it dedups eval batches by game and
this run's 1 level superseded an earlier 2. Its docstring warns that a newer
file is not a better one for EMPTY batches; the same applies to a non-empty
worse batch and the comment does not say so. Verified git-clean first, so no
tracked evidence was overwritten -- the headline moved by aggregation, not loss.

